claimed: merge-scaling-shape — the decisive measurement filed at the end of channel-cas-contention: is !.resume's Bind-rotation cost in the Source path QUADRATIC (left-nested, which reflection-without-remorse / a type-aligned continuation queue would fix, justifying a kernel rewrite) or CONSTANT per element (one closure allocation per step, which such a queue would not help — leaving "fewer widen layers" as the only real lever)? Measured by scaling N across okaySourceSingleDrain (isolated interpretation, no channel/fibers), okaySourceMerge and okayChannelMerge, reading time PER ELEMENT.
